1 Role Management
Purpose
Role Management is used to manage roles in the application and to approve/reject role related requests.
When the user clicks on Role Management from the side bar, the Role Management screen is displayed along with two tabs:
    • Role Management: To manage roles and view the status of role requests.
    • Role Management Requests: To approve/reject pending requests for roles created by users.

When the user clicks on Role Management, two tabs will be displayed:
    • Manage Roles: To create and modify the Role requests.
    • My Requests: To view the status of the requests raised by the user.

    • Manage Roles:

This tab displays all approved (accepted) Roles records in a table format.
Creating a New Role:
    •  Create Flow
 User → Create Role→ Goes to My Requests → Approver Reviews → Approve →    Appears in Manage Roles
Editing/Modify an Existing Role:
    • Update Flow
User → Create/Edit Role → Request Created → Approver Reviews → Approve → Role Updated in Role Management


    • View Role Details
User can view role details using the View.

    • My Requests Tab:

The My Requests tab displays all requests submitted by the logged-in user.
Note: Once approved or rejected, a request cannot be cancelled.

View: Users can view all the request details. 

                                  







2 User Management
Purpose
The User Management module is designed to allow users to create, update, view, approve, reject, and manage User-related information in a structured and controlled workflow.
When the user clicks on User Management from the side bar, the User Management screen is displayed along with two tabs:
    • User Creation: To manage User and view the status of self-requests.
    • User Requests: To approve/reject pending requests for users created by other users.


When the user clicks on User Creation, two tabs will be displayed:
    • Manage Users: To create and modify the User requests.
    • My Requests: To view the status of the requests raised by the same user.

    • Manage Users Tab:

This tab displays all approved (accepted) User records in a table format.
    • Creating a New User:
    • Create Flow
User → Create User → Goes to My Requests → Approver Reviews → Approve →    Appears in Manage Users


Note: Ensure all mandatory fields are completed.
The request is not directly added to the Manage User table. It is sent for approval. The newly created request will appear in the My Requests tab.
    • Editing/Modify an Existing User:
    • Update Flow
User → Edit User→ Goes to My Requests → Approver Reviews → Approve → Updated in Manage Users

After Update, the update is treated as a new request. The modification request appears in the My Requests tab. It must be approved before changes reflect in the main Manage Users list.

    • My Requests Tab:

The My Requests tab displays all requests submitted by the logged-in user.
Note: Once approved or rejected, a request cannot be cancelled.
View: Users can view all the request details.



